        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Plants: Lesquerella, Thujopsis, Paysonia\n- Taxonomy: genus names, plant families, reclassification\n\nFacts:\n- Lesquerella is the former name of a genus of flowering plants in a plant family.\n- Until 2002, Paysonia was considered part of the genus Lesquerella.\n- In 2002, Paysonia was separated from Lesquerella based on genetic and morphological features.\n- Thujopsis is a conifer in the cypress family, Cupressaceae.\n- Thujopsis dolabrata is the sole member of the genus Thujopsis.",
